dialogue cityruins_recruit_healer
title: A healer in the underspire
trigger: ThemeStart cityruins
speaker commander $commander
speaker recruit $recruit
speaker backer $party:2

node meet recruit
  Sit down. You brought the Still's cold out with you. I can see it on your skin.
  -> reply

node reply commander
  The healer is already reaching for a satchel of salves.
  * Thank you. We'll sit. -> sit
  * We don't have time to sit. -> hurry
  * Who are you? -> who

node sit recruit
  Good. Most people down here argue first and sit after they fall over. Hands out. Let me see.
  -> road

node hurry recruit
  Then you have time to fall over. Sit, or I'll be mending you off the floor in an hour.
  -> road

node who recruit
  Somebody who mends people. Down here that's all anybody needs to know about me, and more than most ask.
  -> road

node road commander
  The salve is warm, and smells of lantern oil.
  * That's Lantern Road oil. You're far from the gorges. -> lantern
  * Why mend strangers under the spire? -> strangers

node lantern recruit
  You know the road. Then you know the lanterns burn on mana, same as the neon up there. I came to see what the city does with it.
  -> stair

node strangers recruit
  Because nobody else does. The Street patches its own and the Choir patches nobody. Somebody has to mend the rest.
  -> stair

node stair recruit
  I counted the pilgrims who climbed the stair to the top of the spire. None came down. Now you mean to climb it too.
  -> doubt

node doubt recruit
  Tell me why I should send three more up that stair with my salve still wet on them.
  -> backer

node backer backer
  Because the Commander came out of the Still, and the orbs wake when they're near. We've been mended by worse hands than yours, and we're still walking.
  -> orb

node orb recruit
  Out of the Still. That's why the cold won't leave your skin. And the orb in your hand is glowing like a lantern.
  -> ask

node ask commander
  The light in the orb pulses, slow as a heartbeat.
  * Whatever's at the top drinks the tithe. We mean to stop it. -> stop
  * Walk with us, and nobody climbs alone. -> walk
  * Where we're going is worse than this. -> warned

node stop recruit
  Whatever drinks at the top of that spire has drunk enough. I've buried enough pilgrims to say so.
  -> wagon

node walk recruit
  Nobody climbs alone. The road says that over every lantern. I didn't think I'd hear it under the spire.
  -> wagon

node warned recruit
  Worse than a stair nobody comes down? Then you'll need somebody at the back who means to come down again.
  -> wagon

node wagon recruit
  If your wagon has no seat left, I'll walk behind it with the satchel and come forward when somebody bleeds.
  -> joined

node joined recruit
  Then I'll mend you on the way up. A healer at the back is still a healer.
  do: JoinHero sage role=Healer
  * Glad to have you, Sage. -> welcome
    do: AddTrust $recruit 10
  * Thank the one who vouched for us. -> credit
    do: AddTrust $recruit 5
    do: AddCohesion $recruit $party:2 10
  * Your salve is welcome. Your doubts can stay down here. -> terms
    do: AddTrust $recruit -5
    do: AddCohesion $recruit $party:2 5

node welcome recruit
  Glad to be had. Now hold still, the cold's not out of you yet.

node credit backer
  Someone had to. And I could use the mending, after the Still.
  -> thanks

node thanks recruit
  Then you're first in line. Sit. The road looks after the ones who speak up for it.

node terms recruit
  My doubts come with me. They're what kept me off the stair. I'll mend you anyway.
